: ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.region_geometry", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "The point nearest the intersecting highway before entering the intersection is c's entrance end at r: a halt (drv.motion.complete_halt) with the footprint not overlapping r (rel.occupies), short of r along c's direction (prim.region_offset_along) and with the body within the stop-point tolerance of r (st.region_geometry). The ontology's approach convention reads the edge of the intersection as the carrier's entrance end."}, {"span": "s9", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "The event the halt precedes: the vehicle's footprint comes to overlap the intersection r (rel.occupies true at the observation, false at the previous one), r being the region st.lane_enters names for c."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "s8", "why": "The view of approaching traffic qualifies the third place; the rule takes that place as c's entrance end, the point nearest the intersecting highway before entering, where the view along it is widest, and does not test the view itself (st.sight_along_way is not compared with any bound)."}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) that enters an intersection r at the judged observation t — its footprint overlaps r at t and not at t-1 (rel.occupies) — having occupied at t-1 a carrier c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is r (st.lane_enters(c, r)), and a stop sign (dev.stop_sign) governs c (dev.governs).", "obligation": "Duty of an act before an event (approach convention). Event: the entry into r at t through c; the duty is judged at t. Act: a halt of the subject (drv.motion.complete_halt, speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) at the governing place, 