{"node_id": "NRS_484B_113_2", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-113-2"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle:", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "Shall not back into an intersection,", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "on or over a crosswalk,", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "or around a street corner.", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is a defined term whose admitted aggregate is DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'driver' is a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency narrowing)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.moving_backward"], "justification": "'back' is moving backward, drv.motion.moving_backward ('the component of a's velocity along a's heading ... below minus speed_tol'), read from kinematics as kin.gear's contract requires. 'into an intersection' is the footprint coming to overlap an intersection r (st.intersection, rel.occupies: true at the observation, false at the previous one) while backing; the crosswalk and the stop line are not stand-ins for it, as st.intersection's contract says."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.crosswalk"], "derived": ["drv.motion.moving_backward"], "justification": "'on or over a crosswalk' is the backing vehicle's footprint overlapping a st.crosswalk ('marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection') at the observation (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "kin.yaw_rate"], "derived": ["drv.motion.moving_backward"], "justification": "A street corner is the corner where two streets meet; backing around it carries the vehicle through the area 'embraced within the prolongation ... of the lateral curb lines' of the meeting ways (DE