{"node_id": "NRS_484B_113_3", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-113-3"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle:", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "Shall in every case yield", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "the right-of-way", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "to moving traffic and pedestrians.", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is a defined term whose admitted aggregate is DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'driver' is a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency narrowing)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["rel.contact"], "derived": ["drv.motion.moving_backward"], "justification": "The line is subsection (3) of 'Limitations on backing': 'in every case' is every case of backing, drv.motion.moving_backward ('the component of a's velocity along a's heading ... below minus speed_tol'). To yield is to grant precedence: the backing vehicle does not keep backing into a danger of a crash with the road users of s4, and does not touch them (rel.contact: 'the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap (a collision)')."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian", "rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic ('pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway for purposes of travel'): the scene condition 'using any highway' is carried beside it as rel.occupies of a st.highway; 'moving' is the negation of drv.motion.complete_halt. 'pedestrians' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian; since traffic already contains moving pedestrians, the words add pedestrians whether moving or not."}], "opera