{"node_id": "NRS_484B_113_2", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-113-2"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle:", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "Shall not back into an intersection, on or over a crosswalk, or around a street corner.", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is a defined term whose admitted aggregate is DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'driver' is a role read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency narrowing)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.crosswalk", "kin.yaw_rate"], "derived": ["drv.motion.moving_backward"], "justification": "'back' is moving backward, drv.motion.moving_backward ('the component of a's velocity along a's heading ... below minus speed_tol'), read from kinematics as kin.gear's contract requires. 'into an intersection' is the footprint coming to overlap an intersection r (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'; rel.occupies true at the observation, false at the previous one) while backing; the crosswalk and the stop line are not stand-ins for it, as st.intersection's contract says. 'on or over a crosswalk' is the backing vehicle's footprint overlapping a st.crosswalk ('marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection'). 'around a street corner': the corner is where two streets meet; backing around it carries the vehicle through the area 'embraced within the prolongation ... of the lateral curb lines' of the meeting ways (DEF-NRS-484A-105), the st.intersection region, while its heading turns — read as backing with the footprint overlapping r, the heading having changed by at least the turn threshold since the backing within r began (Term.headingSince, integrated from kin.yaw_rate)."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) that is backing at the observation: drv.motion.moving_backward(subject) with speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance.", "obligation": "At the observation, none of: (a) for some intersection r (st.intersection), the subject's footprint overlaps r and did not at the previous observation (rel.occupies) — it backs into r; (b) for some crosswalk x (st.crosswalk), the footprint overlaps x (rel.occupies); (c) for some intersection r, the footprint overlaps r and the magnitude of Term.headingSince(subject, p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph, ψ) is at least p.turn_heading_min, where ψ = drv.motion.moving_backward(subject) and rel.occupies(subject, r): since it last began backing within r its heading has turned at least by the turn threshold — it backs around the corner.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_heading_min"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'back into an intersection' is read as the entry into the intersection while backing; backing straight out of an intersection the vehicle is already in is not backing into it."}, {"span": "s4", "why": "'around a street corner' is read through the intersection region the corner bounds, with a heading change of at least p.turn_heading_min while backing within it; the city-limit qualifier of 'street' (DEF-NRS-484A-265) is not read, every intersection's corners being treated as street corners."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car backs at 2 m/s along a street and its footprint comes to overlap the i