tance (st.region_geometry) is at most p.stop_point_tolerance; (2) else, where the crosswalk lists are observed and none marks c, and a stop line l is recorded as marking c: a halt at which the subject is not past l along c's direction and the body-to-l distance is at most p.stop_point_tolerance; (3) else, where the crosswalk and stop-line lists are observed and none marks c: a halt at which the footprint does not overlap r, the subject is short of r along c's direction, and the body-to-r distance is at most p.stop_point_tolerance. Where several marks of the governing kind mark c, a halt in the zone of any of them it has not passed counts. History bound: the search runs back from t-1 and ends at the approach start — the last observation before t at which the subject, on a carrier the governing mark is recorded as marking, is outside that mark's stopping zone upstream (off the mark, short of it, farther than p.stop_point_tolerance; with several marks, outside and short of each) — or at the subject's previous entry into r, whichever is later. Nothing else ends it: not the start of the recording, a first observation, another intersection or mark, or a distance travelled. Crossing the mark, moving on toward r, a change of carrier or lateral move within the same entry, a reverse within the zone and speed noise begin no new approach; only an observed exit from the zone upstream does. Verdict: the act found → compliant; the search reaches the approach start or the previous entry without it → violated; it reaches neither without the act → unknown. Missing evidence: the entry is unknown, never absent, where t-1 does not show the subject on a mapped carrier with an observed association to r; an unobserved dev.governs of c, an unobserved association of a mark with c, or an unobserved closest approach makes the verdict unknown only where it turns on it — a halt found at a place known to govern is compliant whatever the conflict reading, and a duty that does not arise is decided 