e within which two bodies collide or nearly collide", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) that enters an intersection r at the judged observation t — its footprint overlaps r at t and not at t-1 (rel.occupies) — having occupied at t-1 a carrier c (st.travel_region) whose entrance end is r (st.lane_enters(c, r)) and which a yield sign (dev.yield_sign) governs (dev.governs); and a stop was required for safety: at some observation from the approach start (as defined in the obligation) to t-1, some road user u other than the subject (not same) that is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) occupying a highway (rel.occupies, st.highway) satisfies prim.closest_approach_within(subject, u, p.conflict_horizon) and prim.closest_approach_distance(subject, u, p.conflict_horizon) < p.conflict_centre_clearance. Where no observation of that stretch shows such a road user, the duty does not arise.", "obligation": "Duty of an act before an event (approach convention). Event: the entry into r at t through c; the duty is judged at t. Act: a halt of the subject (drv.motion.complete_halt, speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) at the governing place, read through c. Place, in the order the words list: (1) where a crosswalk x is recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of(x, c)): a halt at which the footprint does not overlap x (rel.occupies), the subject is short of x along c's designated direction (prim.region_offset_along of x along st.lane_direction of c, positive) and the body-to-x ground distance (st.region_geometry) is at most p.stop_point_tolerance; (2) else, where the crosswalk lists are observed and none marks c, and a stop line l is recorded as marking c: a halt at which the subject is not past l along c's direction and the body-to-l distanc