 vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'approaching a yield sign' is read through a yield sign the source records as governing the approach carrier c that enters r; a sign recorded only as governing the intersection itself is not read as facing c.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s6", "why": "'clearly marked' is read by the represented stop line; the paint's clarity is not modelled.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s8", "why": "The point nearest the intersecting highway is read as c's entrance end, the edge of r, within p.stop_point_tolerance; the view of approaching traffic at that point is not tested (residue s9)."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car on lane c, governed by a yield sign, with a crosswalk marking c, approaches at 10 m/s while a car on the crossing highway is on a closest approach with it 2 s ahead at 1 m; the car never comes to rest and enters the intersection."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Same conflict; the car comes to rest 1 m short of the crosswalk, off it, lets the crossing car pass, and enters."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The car approaches the yield sign alone in the scene, no road user is ever on a closest approach with it, and it enters without halting: no stop was required for safety."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As in forbid, but the source does not observe which travel regions the yield sign governs.", "masked": ["dev.governs"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "No crosswalk marks c (lists observed); a stop line marks c; with the conflict present, the car comes to rest 1 m short of the line and then enters."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Neither a crosswalk nor a stop line marks c (lists observed); with the conflict present, the car comes to rest 1 m short of the intersection's edge, off it, and then enters."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A crosswalk marks c; the conflict is present on the approach; the car rests 20 m short of the crosswalk, moves on and enters without halting again."}, {"name": "history_boundary", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The recording begins with the car already 1 m short of the crosswalk marking c, moving at 3 m/s, while a crossing car is on a closest approach with it 2 s ahead at 1 m; it enters without a recorded halt and no recorded observation shows it outside the stopping zone upstream.", "boundary": "the approach start: the observation at which the car was outside the crosswalk's stopping zone upstream lies before the recording, so whether it halted within the zone before the recording began is not observed"}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; speed resolution of the acquisition standard"}, {"name": "p.stop_point_tolerance", "unit": "m", "value": 2.0, "convention": "the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin", "source": "proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_20_060_o1; MUTCD stop-line placement before a crosswalk"}, {"name": "p.conflict_horizon", "unit": "s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash", "source": "proposed this iteration by LVMC_11_12_070_B; traffic-conflict technique TTC thresholds"}, {"name": "p.conflict_centre_clearance", "unit": "m", "value": 3.0, "convention": "centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodie